course: dictionary
lesson: 12967
title: Showing by example
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Exemplify is a formal word. It means to be a perfect example of something, or to give an example to show what you mean. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Her kindness exemplifies what a good friend should be.» Her kindness is a perfect example of a good friend, so exemplifies means is a typical example of.
explain: Sometimes the word shows that you are giving an example. «The teacher exemplified good manners by always saying please and thank you.» The teacher did not just talk about manners. She showed them by doing them, so exemplified means showed by example.
explain: In exam questions you may see «Which sentence best exemplifies…?» This means «Which is the best example of…?» Ask yourself: which choice clearly shows the quality named? Then check your answer by swapping in the simpler words.
fact: Exemplify means to be a typical example of something, or to give an example to show what you mean.
fact: Exemplify is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in essays, stories and exam questions.
fact: Common phrases are exemplify a quality, and is exemplified by, as in «Courage is exemplified by the firefighters who go into the smoke.»
fact: «Which sentence best exemplifies…?» means «Which is the best example of…?»
exercise: «Her kindness exemplifies what a good friend should be.» What does exemplifies mean here? | Is hidden under | Is afraid of | Ignores | *Is a perfect example of
exercise: «The teacher exemplified good manners by always saying please and thank you.» What did the teacher do? | Slept during the lesson | *Showed good manners by doing them | Shouted at the class | Forgot all the rules
exercise: In a test you see «Which sentence best exemplifies honesty?» What is it asking? | Which sentence is the shortest? | *Which sentence is the best example of honesty? | Which sentence is the longest? | Which sentence has the most adjectives?
test: Mum says, «Your sharing exemplifies what kindness is.» What is she saying? | *Your sharing is a perfect example of kindness | Your sharing has ended | Your sharing is too loud | Your sharing is hidden from view
test: Fill the gap: «The story ___ what courage really means.» | hides | *exemplifies | forgets | argues
exam: Which of these best exemplifies honesty? | A child who runs away from the mess | *A child who owns up to breaking the vase | A child who blames the dog | A child who hides the broken pieces
